      "id": "3q0thmi",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Acids"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Acids taste sour, turn blue litmus red, and release H+ ions in aqueous solutions.",
        "Bases taste bitter, feel soapy, turn red litmus blue, and release OH- ions in aqueous solutions.",
        "Alkalis are water-soluble bases such as Sodium Hydroxide (NaOH) and Potassium Hydroxide (KOH).",
        "A neutralization reaction between an acid and a base produces salt and water.",
        "The pH scale measures the concentration of hydrogen ions, where a lower pH indicates higher acidity."
      ],
      "id": "42emx0x"
    },
